  "accessibility": {
    "voiceOver": true,
    "dynamicType": true,
    "reduceMotion": true,
    "notes": "VoiceOver reads the button's label in every state, adds the system's \"in progress\" description while the action runs, and announces the result (\"Done\" or \"Failed\" by default; see VoiceOver announcements above). Success and failure play haptics. Reduce Motion turns the press scale into a brief dim, removes the failure shake and cross-fades state changes. The button sizes to its label through the largest Dynamic Type sizes and keeps the same size in every state."
  }
